or"><name><surname>Rasmussen</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Evaluation of Gaussian Processes and Other Methods for Nonlinear                        Regression &#x0005b;PhD thesis&#x0005d;. Toronto, Canada: Department of                        Computer Science, University of Toronto.</article-title><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cs.utoronto.ca/~carl">http://www.cs.utoronto.ca/~carl</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000211-Kim1"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>H-C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Bayesian Gaussian process classification with the EM-EP                        algorithm.</article-title><source>IEEE Trans Pattern Anal Mach Intell</source><volume>28(12)</volume><fpage>1948</fpage><lpage>1959</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17108369</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000211-Kalman1"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kalman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1960</year><article-title>A new approach to linear filtering and prediction problems.</article-title><source>ASME Trans J Basic Eng</source><volume>82(1)</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>45</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000211-Wang1"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Variational Bayesian inference for partially observed diffusions.                        Technical Report 04-4, University of Glasgow.</article-title><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.stats.gla.ac.uk/Research/-TechRep2003/04-4.pdf">http://www.stats.gla.ac.uk/Research/-TechRep2003/04-4.pdf</ext-